/// The hero: a Mixamo Swat Guy, baked to the §1 contract by
/// `vrm-pipeline/bake_hero.py` (12 standard-name clips, scale normalized at
/// bake time) with the sword attached by `vrm-pipeline/attach_sword.py`.
/// The swords are deliberately oversized (the standard blade is 1.45 m,
/// bright steel): at the real 0.95 m the sword was invisible on the
/// phone screen (2026-11-14 device check), so it follows the survivor
/// guns' "bigger than life" rule. Visual only — no combat number reads
/// the mesh. There is exactly one bake of the rig (the variation
/// system's per-sword bakes went with it, 2026-11-15). Mixamo-derived,
/// so the GLB stays out of the repo and is bundled locally; when it is
/// not mounted the kit falls back to a capsule hero. The crowd
/// bake is a Mixamo zombie under the same rule.
const HERO_GLB: &str = "assets/models/swat_sword.glb";
const ZOMBIE_GLB: &str = "assets/models/cop_zombie_light.glb";
/// The ground re-skin round (2026-11-20) took the zombie bake
/// out of the preview bundle's enumeration — the 500-file cap is
/// binding and the pack bundles every pose set, so the crowd's
/// transform-only fallback never engages there (the pose path
/// outranks it whenever any set is ready); a build with the file
/// mounted keeps the fallback, and a build with neither falls to
/// capsules, the same posture as the item sword. One manifest
/// line restores it when the budget allows.
/// The Swat bake stands 1.78 m in real metres, so the walker plays it at
/// scale 1 (its armature root carries the usual Mixamo 0.01, which the
/// skinned path composes like the other Mixamo rigs).
const HERO_SCALE: f32 = 1.0;

/// The zombie bake was authored for the skinned walker path: its mesh sits
/// under a Mixamo "Armature" node with scale 0.01 and a -90 deg X-rotation,
/// and the static (Rest) mesh path bakes that world matrix in. As a static
/// prop it comes out 100x too small and lying flat; the prop transform
/// compensates with scale 100 and this pitch. (The hero does not need it:
/// KayKit is authored at a sane scale and plays through the walker path.)
const STAND_PITCH: f32 = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;

/// Pose-baked crowd set (design §1.7), baked by `vrm-pipeline/bake_poses.py`
/// from the Mixamo zombie clips: three characters, eight poses each,
/// normalized at bake time (real metres, feet at the origin, facing +Z —
/// the facing the prop path expects, measured on ZOMBIE_GLB's bind pose).
/// Mixamo-derived, so the GLBs stay out of the repo; when they are absent
/// the kit falls back to ZOMBIE_GLB with transform-only poses, then to
/// capsules.
/// The pose set every crowd kind is baked with (walk cycle, attack,
/// flinch, launched, corpse). The character half of the path is the
/// kind's id — see [`ENEMY_KINDS`].
const POSE_NAMES: [&str; 8] = [
    "walk0", "walk1", "walk2", "walk3", "attack", "hit", "fly", "die",
];
const POSE_ATTACK: usize = 4;
const POSE_HIT: usize = 5;
const POSE_FLY: usize = 6;
const POSE_DIE: usize = 7;

fn pose_path(char: &str, pose: &str) -> String {
    format!("assets/models/poses/{char}_{pose}.glb")
}

